789
00:48:14,322 --> 00:48:16,306
Robbie Rivers, WFPO.
May I ask...

790
00:48:16,433 --> 00:48:18,257
Fuck the fuck off.
Okay.

791
00:48:18,385 --> 00:48:21,073
You two are a familiar sight.
What are you doing in town?

792
00:48:21,840 --> 00:48:22,930
Just passing through.

793
00:48:23,057 --> 00:48:24,338
With Gale Weathers?

794
00:48:24,464 --> 00:48:27,313
And you just happened
to run over
an escaped mental patient

795
00:48:27,440 --> 00:48:29,296
in front of Sidney Evans's home?

796
00:48:29,425 --> 00:48:31,088
What's really going on here?

797
00:48:31,216 --> 00:48:32,666
Why don't you
get your own story, Robbie.

798
00:48:32,689 --> 00:48:34,898
Yeah, we're not here
to do it for you.

799
00:48:35,794 --> 00:48:38,800
Come on, give a small-town
reporter his big break!

800
00:48:42,418 --> 00:48:44,785
Hey, Sidney.

801
00:48:44,912 --> 00:48:47,760
I'm so sorry this is happening
again, Mrs. Prescott.

802
00:48:48,689 --> 00:48:50,320
Mrs. Evans, Lucas.

803
00:48:50,449 --> 00:48:52,369
Right, yeah. Uh...

804
00:48:52,496 --> 00:48:53,777
Sorry, that's what I meant.

805
00:48:54,512 --> 00:48:56,144
Lucas, do you know
anything about A.I.?

806
00:48:56,273 --> 00:48:58,450
A.I.? Uh, I refuse.

807
00:48:58,577 --> 00:49:01,169
That is the death
of civilization.

808
00:49:01,297 --> 00:49:03,250
Why are you asking that?

809
00:49:03,984 --> 00:49:05,297
Just be careful, Jess.

810
00:49:05,425 --> 00:49:06,833
Keep your doors locked.

811
00:49:08,402 --> 00:49:10,609
Okay, come on, let's go.

812
00:49:13,520 --> 00:49:14,671
Oh, you're Gale Weathers. Hey.

813
00:49:14,737 --> 00:49:16,945
And who are you?
Uh...

814
00:49:17,360 --> 00:49:18,546
I'm Lucas.

815
00:49:19,120 --> 00:49:20,209
What are you doing here?

816
00:49:20,336 --> 00:49:22,482
He's my son,
and we live next door.

817
00:49:22,609 --> 00:49:24,272
We're friends
of the family.
Hmm.

818
00:49:24,402 --> 00:49:25,393
Yeah.

819
00:49:26,000 --> 00:49:27,633
You like horror movies, Lucas?

820
00:49:27,760 --> 00:49:29,585
Yeah, I lo... I love them.

821
00:49:29,713 --> 00:49:31,345
Especially the Stab movies?

822
00:49:31,473 --> 00:49:32,701
Yeah,
I know them inside and out.

823
00:49:32,816 --> 00:49:34,704
What are you doing?
Mom, it's Gale Weathers.

824
00:49:34,832 --> 00:49:37,937
The Stab movies were based
on her true crime bestseller,
The Woodsboro Murders.

825
00:49:38,065 --> 00:49:40,593
I know, but I don't like
the way she's looking at you.

826
00:49:40,721 --> 00:49:44,113
Please leave my son out of
whatever it is you're doing.

827
00:49:45,073 --> 00:49:46,064
Sorry, kid,

828
00:49:46,193 --> 00:49:47,698
but you know how this works.

829
00:49:47,825 --> 00:49:48,784
Yeah.

830
00:49:48,848 --> 00:49:50,993
Everyone's a suspect.

831
00:49:51,120 --> 00:49:54,449
Well, yeah, but you killed
the killer. He's dead.

832
00:49:54,578 --> 00:49:55,760
Hmm.

833
00:49:56,784 --> 00:49:58,800
How do you know
there's just one?

834
00:50:00,242 --> 00:50:01,201
Excuse me.

835
00:50:01,265 --> 00:50:03,218
Whoa.

836
00:50:03,344 --> 00:50:07,153
Until this is over, I want you
to stay away from this house.

837
00:50:07,793 --> 00:50:09,104
Come on, let's go.

838
00:50:14,000 --> 00:50:15,698
How did you know to come?

839
00:50:15,824 --> 00:50:18,578
When the news broke
about the two murders
at the Macher house,

840
00:50:18,704 --> 00:50:21,937
a flock of reporters
raced to get there, but...

841
00:50:22,066 --> 00:50:24,433
my Sidney-sense told me
that Woodsboro was played out.

842
00:50:24,560 --> 00:50:28,496
Mark is having
the recorded calls analyzed
to confirm they're fake.

843
00:50:28,626 --> 00:50:30,641
Is it possible they're real?

844
00:50:30,769 --> 00:50:32,144
Could Stu be alive?

845
00:50:32,273 --> 00:50:36,241
That would be
the better story,
but it's... too far-fetched.

846
00:50:36,370 --> 00:50:37,361
Hmm.

847
00:50:40,497 --> 00:50:41,680
What's going on?

848
00:50:41,808 --> 00:50:44,337
Oh, I just have
some nerve damage from the...

849
00:50:44,465 --> 00:50:46,385
from the attack in New York.

850
00:50:46,513 --> 00:50:47,707
You're lucky you sat
that one out.

851
00:50:47,730 --> 00:50:49,584
It-It was brutal.

852
00:50:50,225 --> 00:50:51,185
Thank you.

853
00:50:51,313 --> 00:50:52,561
It's nice to meet you, Tatum.

854
00:50:52,690 --> 00:50:54,416
Mmm. Tatum?

855
00:50:55,248 --> 00:50:56,913
Tatum as in...
That Tatum.

856
00:50:57,040 --> 00:50:58,160
Yeah.

857
00:50:58,290 --> 00:50:59,569
What do you two do for Gale?

858
00:50:59,697 --> 00:51:00,913
We're her hot interns.

859
00:51:01,040 --> 00:51:02,513
Ever since she got axed,

860
00:51:02,642 --> 00:51:04,241
she's been trying to
go back to her roots.

861
00:51:04,369 --> 00:51:07,153
So she's rebranding herself
as a crime reporter.

862
00:51:07,282 --> 00:51:08,858
She's teaching us
all she knows about the biz.

863
00:51:08,881 --> 00:51:10,640
Don't say "biz."
Yep.

864
00:51:10,770 --> 00:51:13,520
It's more like we're showing
Gale the ropes
of making premium content.

865
00:51:13,650 --> 00:51:14,929
Don't say "content."

866
00:51:15,057 --> 00:51:16,368
It's going great.

867
00:51:16,497 --> 00:51:17,658
Except Mindy keeps trying to
steal Gale's thunder.

868
00:51:17,681 --> 00:51:19,697
I'm the face of the future.
Sure.

869
00:51:19,825 --> 00:51:22,546
But in the meantime,
we're learning all about
fading careers

870
00:51:22,673 --> 00:51:24,210
and failed comebacks.

871
00:51:25,904 --> 00:51:27,313
Where are we gonna start?

872
00:51:28,113 --> 00:51:30,833
S-Start what? I'm...

873
00:51:32,081 --> 00:51:33,393
I'm not starting anything.

874
00:51:33,520 --> 00:51:35,793
We have to find out
who's behind this.

875
00:51:35,921 --> 00:51:37,360
That guy in the road,
Karl Gibbs,

876
00:51:37,488 --> 00:51:38,801
is not some random killer.

877
00:51:38,929 --> 00:51:41,393
It's always someone
connected to your past.

878
00:51:41,521 --> 00:51:42,833
The police can handle it.

879
00:51:42,962 --> 00:51:44,208
That would be your husband.

880
00:51:44,337 --> 00:51:45,682
And we need to help him.

881
00:51:46,450 --> 00:51:48,145
Don't you want to
know who's behind this?

882
00:51:48,273 --> 00:51:50,482
Gale, I can't anymore.

883
00:51:50,609 --> 00:51:53,776
I need to be with my family,
I need to know they're safe.

884
00:51:53,905 --> 00:51:55,094
That's why you need to help me.

885
00:51:55,186 --> 00:51:57,458
Whoever is targeting you
is not gonna stop...

886
00:51:57,584 --> 00:51:59,153
you know that.

887
00:52:03,122 --> 00:52:06,801
Oh, slap my face, if it
isn't the Gale Weathers!

888
00:52:06,929 --> 00:52:08,080
Hi. Oh, my God,

889
00:52:08,208 --> 00:52:10,160
I am so sorry
your show got canceled

890
00:52:10,290 --> 00:52:11,953
and then you got fired.

891
00:52:12,080 --> 00:52:14,353
I wasn't fired.
My contract wasn't renewed.

892
00:52:14,481 --> 00:52:16,914
So don't care.
Not even a little.

893
00:52:17,041 --> 00:52:19,760
Ugh. I'm so sorry for
running over your friend.

894
00:52:19,890 --> 00:52:21,714
Can't do your own
dirty work, Stu?

895
00:52:23,378 --> 00:52:24,625
Neither can you.

896
00:52:24,753 --> 00:52:27,857
You brought in some old,
irrelevant hag for backup.

897
00:52:27,985 --> 00:52:29,138
It's so sad.

898
00:52:29,264 --> 00:52:30,587
And what happened to
the two of you?

899
00:52:30,610 --> 00:52:32,240
You both had so much spunk.

900
00:52:32,370 --> 00:52:34,609
You're gonna die,
you A.I. asshole.

901
00:52:34,737 --> 00:52:36,337
We're going to see how fake I am

902
00:52:36,466 --> 00:52:38,417
when I stab you
in the fucking throat!

903
00:52:38,545 --> 00:52:39,888
Because I'm coming for you

904
00:52:40,017 --> 00:52:43,313
and I'm gonna love
every second of it.

905
00:52:48,145 --> 00:52:49,873
That was fucking weird.

906
00:52:52,625 --> 00:52:54,354
Fallbrook Psychiatric Hospital.

907
00:52:54,481 --> 00:52:56,657
It's a couple hours away.
We'll start there.

908
00:52:58,128 --> 00:52:59,313
There she is.

909
00:53:00,081 --> 00:53:01,778
I knew you were
in there somewhere.

910
00:53:01,904 --> 00:53:05,297
You're right. This isn't
gonna stop unless I stop it.

911
00:53:12,305 --> 00:53:13,969
I'll be back as soon as I can.

912
00:53:14,097 --> 00:53:15,953
Mom, I want to go with you.

913
00:53:16,082 --> 00:53:17,873
No, sweetie, it's not safe.

914
00:53:18,002 --> 00:53:18,961
So why are you going?

915
00:53:19,057 --> 00:53:20,057
Because I know what I'm doing.

916
00:53:20,080 --> 00:53:21,234
Mom, please.

917
00:53:21,361 --> 00:53:22,714
You don't have
the skill set for this.

918
00:53:22,737 --> 00:53:24,305
Well, then show me.

919
00:53:25,105 --> 00:53:27,250
I don't want to end up like
the other Tatum.

920
00:53:28,497 --> 00:53:29,680
What?

921
00:53:30,482 --> 00:53:31,594
You named me after a girl who

922
00:53:31,664 --> 00:53:33,970
got her head crushed
in a garage door.

923
00:53:34,097 --> 00:53:36,145
She was my friend.
And she's dead!

924
00:53:37,777 --> 00:53:39,474
She was a-a victim,
not a fighter.

925
00:53:39,601 --> 00:53:41,905
I want to be a fighter.

926
00:53:42,033 --> 00:53:43,505
Honey. Listen...

927
00:53:43,633 --> 00:53:45,329
Nice to know what
you think of me.

928
00:53:54,001 --> 00:53:57,169
She just lost a friend,
so... she's upset.

929
00:53:58,129 --> 00:53:59,761
I want you to keep
her away from Ben.

930
00:53:59,890 --> 00:54:01,905
He's not to come over here.

931
00:54:02,033 --> 00:54:04,817
Someone was hiding
in the attic.
It could have been him.

932
00:54:04,945 --> 00:54:09,234
We are running traces on
all her friends' cell numbers,
emails and IP's.

933
00:54:09,361 --> 00:54:12,529
If Ben or any of her friends
are connected in any way

934
00:54:12,657 --> 00:54:13,840
we're gonna find it.

935
00:54:16,945 --> 00:54:20,369
She's right, you know.
Me protecting her from this,

936
00:54:21,010 --> 00:54:22,737
I made her vulnerable to it.

937
00:54:44,050 --> 00:54:45,041
Right.

938
00:54:46,257 --> 00:54:47,440
Okay.

939
00:54:48,241 --> 00:54:50,833
Okay, Terry. Thanks again.

940
00:54:52,913 --> 00:54:55,921
Woodsboro coroner says
there's no intake form
on Stu Macher's body.

941
00:54:56,048 --> 00:54:59,249
The woman who was coroner
in '96 died three years ago,

942
00:54:59,377 --> 00:55:00,401
so there's no one to ask.

943
00:55:00,529 --> 00:55:03,345
So it's a case
of lost paperwork?

944
00:55:03,473 --> 00:55:04,753
Or stolen paperwork.

945
00:55:04,881 --> 00:55:06,554
Someone who wants to
make it look like Stu's body

946
00:55:06,577 --> 00:55:08,050
never made it to the morgue.

947
00:55:09,233 --> 00:55:10,192
Or...

948
00:55:10,257 --> 00:55:11,473
It's actually Stu.

949
00:55:11,601 --> 00:55:13,457
Let's find out.
Yep.

950
00:55:14,288 --> 00:55:15,569
Here's your pass.
Thank you.

951
00:55:16,113 --> 00:55:17,072
Here you go.

952
00:55:17,137 --> 00:55:18,321
Thanks.

953
00:55:19,249 --> 00:55:20,689
How can I help you?

954
00:55:20,817 --> 00:55:21,968
Hi, I'm Gale Weathers.

955
00:55:22,097 --> 00:55:23,761
I'm a reporter
for Channel 7 in New York.

956
00:55:23,888 --> 00:55:25,169
Mm-hmm.

957
00:55:25,297 --> 00:55:26,946
We're doing a story
on Karl Gibbs.
I figured.

958
00:55:26,993 --> 00:55:30,417
The state police,
they were here all night
going through his stuff.

959
00:55:30,929 --> 00:55:32,113
Can we see his room?

960
00:55:32,657 --> 00:55:33,841
Well...

961
00:55:37,169 --> 00:55:39,729
Yeah, I guess so. Come on,
it's right down this way.

962
00:55:40,785 --> 00:55:42,801
So what can you
tell us about Karl?

963
00:55:42,929 --> 00:55:44,529
He was a pretty violent guy.

964
00:55:45,553 --> 00:55:48,561
Killed three women
about 20 years ago.

965
00:55:51,217 --> 00:55:52,849
Can you think of any reason
that he would

966
00:55:52,977 --> 00:55:55,057
go after Sidney Prescott
and her family?

967
00:55:56,049 --> 00:55:57,969
No, not that I know of.

968
00:55:59,089 --> 00:56:00,689
I'm glad you're okay, though.

969
00:56:01,169 --> 00:56:02,705
Thanks.

970
00:56:05,745 --> 00:56:08,593
Did you ever hear him talk
about the Ghostface killings?

971
00:56:08,721 --> 00:56:11,505
Or the Stab movies,
or anything like that?

972
00:56:11,633 --> 00:56:12,689
Not that I remember.

973
00:56:12,817 --> 00:56:14,161
What about, um...

974
00:56:14,769 --> 00:56:15,728
him?

975
00:56:15,793 --> 00:56:17,905
Yeah, that's John.

976
00:56:18,737 --> 00:56:19,825
John?

977
00:56:19,953 --> 00:56:21,265
Yeah, as in John Doe.

978
00:56:21,393 --> 00:56:22,961
He didn't know his real name.

979
00:56:23,089 --> 00:56:24,585
He had amnesia from
the blow to the head

980
00:56:24,689 --> 00:56:26,449
that gave him all those scars.

981
00:56:26,577 --> 00:56:28,017
When did he arrive here?

982
00:56:28,145 --> 00:56:29,457
Well, it was before my time.

983
00:56:29,585 --> 00:56:33,873
I've been here 16 years.
So late '90s, maybe?

984
00:56:34,769 --> 00:56:37,169
His room was right down there.
You want to see it?

985
00:56:37,297 --> 00:56:38,513
Yes.

986
00:56:38,641 --> 00:56:40,401
You know, h-he was a drifter.

987
00:56:40,529 --> 00:56:43,569
Sleeping on the streets
of California or somewhere.

988
00:56:44,561 --> 00:56:46,769
And then one day he snapped.

989
00:56:47,409 --> 00:56:49,553
Attacked a high school girl.

990
00:56:49,681 --> 00:56:53,649
He was declared incompetent to
stand trial and ended up here.

991
00:56:54,481 --> 00:56:57,073
And where is he now?
He was released.

992
00:56:58,641 --> 00:57:00,369
Two weeks ago.

993
00:57:00,497 --> 00:57:02,896
Any idea where he went
after he was released?

994
00:57:03,793 --> 00:57:04,752
No, I'm sorry.

995
00:57:04,816 --> 00:57:05,841
But for that information

996
00:57:05,969 --> 00:57:07,889
you're gonna need a court order.

997
00:57:08,017 --> 00:57:10,353
And I assume that John Doe
and Karl Gibbs

998
00:57:10,481 --> 00:57:11,793
spent a lot of time together?

999
00:57:11,921 --> 00:57:14,129
Oh, yeah.
No, they were good friends.

1000
00:57:14,258 --> 00:57:15,281
Yeah.

1001
00:57:15,409 --> 00:57:16,753
Very close.

1002
00:57:18,961 --> 00:57:20,145
Hmm.

1003
00:57:31,473 --> 00:57:32,656
Hmm.

1004
00:57:35,346 --> 00:57:36,465
Neighbor boy's sus.

1005
00:57:36,593 --> 00:57:38,737
He's out there
staring at the house.

1006
00:57:38,865 --> 00:57:40,114
Not subtle at all.

1007
00:57:40,689 --> 00:57:43,026
I've gone back three days.

1008
00:57:43,153 --> 00:57:44,538
If the killer was hiding
in the attic,

1009
00:57:44,561 --> 00:57:46,193
he had to go into
the house at some point.

1010
00:57:46,321 --> 00:57:48,337
Could the footage be hacked?

1011
00:57:48,465 --> 00:57:50,321
Clearly the killer
is tech savvy.

1012
00:57:50,449 --> 00:57:51,601
I don't know.

1013
00:57:51,729 --> 00:57:53,776
Uh, did you two find the towels?

1014
00:57:53,905 --> 00:57:54,969
You got everything you need?

1015
00:57:54,992 --> 00:57:56,753
Yeah, the water pressure was...

1016
00:57:56,881 --> 00:57:58,673
top-notch, so, thank you.

1017
00:57:58,801 --> 00:58:00,401
Yeah. Yeah, of course.

1018
00:58:01,169 --> 00:58:02,577
So, um...

1019
00:58:03,376 --> 00:58:04,592
Why are you here?

1020
00:58:05,617 --> 00:58:08,432
I'm sorry, I mean, um...

1021
00:58:09,744 --> 00:58:11,409
After everything
you've been through,

1022
00:58:12,113 --> 00:58:13,072
aren't you scared?

1023
00:58:13,137 --> 00:58:15,537
Scared. Necessity.

1024
00:58:15,666 --> 00:58:18,801
My career trajectory
is to succeed
and exceed Gale Weathers.

1025
00:58:18,929 --> 00:58:21,872
And as Woodsboro legacy,
it is our duty.

1026
00:58:22,929 --> 00:58:25,137
Our uncle Randy was really
good friends with your mom.

1027
00:58:25,266 --> 00:58:28,017
And I want to uncover
the killer this time.

1028
00:58:28,146 --> 00:58:29,296
She has been wrong a lot.

1029
00:58:29,425 --> 00:58:30,641
That is not supportive.

1030
00:58:30,769 --> 00:58:33,874
Un-Uncover a killer?
How do you uncover a killer?

1031
00:58:34,000 --> 00:58:38,129
Assemble the suspects
and then Agatha Christie them
until they break.

1032
00:58:38,257 --> 00:58:39,825
So... How do you
know who they are?

1033
00:58:39,953 --> 00:58:42,609
If history is any indication,
it's likely
one of your friends.

1034
00:58:42,736 --> 00:58:43,825
Probably your boyfriend.

1035
00:58:43,952 --> 00:58:45,489
Boyfriend's too obvious.

1036
00:58:45,616 --> 00:58:47,088
Unless it's by design.

1037
00:58:47,217 --> 00:58:48,177
It's not my boyfriend.

1038
00:58:48,306 --> 00:58:49,649
That's cute.

1039
00:58:49,777 --> 00:58:51,578
We need to gather all the
suspects together in one room.

1040
00:58:51,601 --> 00:58:55,345
Well, there's
a curfew at sundown.
The whole town's closing up.

1041
00:58:57,361 --> 00:58:58,737
Actually, there might be a way.

1042
00:58:58,866 --> 00:59:01,553
I just would have to figure
out how to get around my dad.

1043
00:59:01,682 --> 00:59:03,408
Is that possible?

1044
00:59:03,537 --> 00:59:05,137
He is the police chief.

1045
00:59:05,265 --> 00:59:08,145
But if we can find out
who's doing this,
then he can go get them.

1046
00:59:08,273 --> 00:59:09,937
If we can help, we should.

1047
00:59:11,921 --> 00:59:13,360
I'm sick of being useless.

1048
00:59:15,569 --> 00:59:16,978
That was Deputy Cooke.

1049
00:59:17,105 --> 00:59:19,505
They're set up to trace his
phone if he calls me again.

1050
00:59:19,633 --> 00:59:21,489
So we just have to
wait for him to call?

1051
00:59:21,617 --> 00:59:24,433
Oh, come on,
there's got to be some way to
bait him into calling you.

1052
00:59:25,778 --> 00:59:29,328
What if I gave you what you've
been asking me for since 1996?

1053
00:59:30,578 --> 00:59:31,761
An interview.

1054
00:59:33,872 --> 00:59:35,761
Get the fuck out of here.

1055
00:59:35,889 --> 00:59:37,777
Look, I just need an ETA
on that court order.

1056
00:59:37,905 --> 00:59:39,825
You got it, Chief.
I'll take care of it.

1057
00:59:39,953 --> 00:59:42,609
Good. Okay. Call me
the second Sid's phone rings.

1058
00:59:44,145 --> 00:59:45,104
Tatum!

1059
01:02:07,472 --> 01:02:09,874
Okay.
Get home safe. Bye, guys.

1060
01:02:36,785 --> 01:02:37,840
Hey.
Hey, Chlo.

1061
01:02:37,969 --> 01:02:39,185
Ben and Lucas are already here.

1062
01:02:39,312 --> 01:02:42,322
All right. Uh,
this is Chad and Mindy.

1063
01:02:42,449 --> 01:02:44,242
Hi. I'm Chloe. Come on in.

1064
01:02:46,066 --> 01:02:47,952
So your parents own this place.

1065
01:02:48,082 --> 01:02:50,641
Yes, but they
don't know we're here,
so we got to lay low.

1066
01:02:51,440 --> 01:02:52,625
How you doing?

1067
01:02:53,489 --> 01:02:55,280
What are we drinking, kids?

1068
01:02:56,209 --> 01:02:57,425
Here is...

1069
01:02:57,553 --> 01:02:59,794
the
pepperoni and mushroom pizza.

1070
01:02:59,920 --> 01:03:01,265
- Thanks, Chlo.
- Thank you.

1071
01:03:01,393 --> 01:03:03,056
So what is the deal
with you two?

1072
01:03:03,185 --> 01:03:05,905
Um, they want to help
us find out who's doing this.

1073
01:03:06,032 --> 01:03:08,912
What, they think it's one of us?

1074
01:03:12,082 --> 01:03:14,384
Yeah. But I don't.

1075
01:03:15,601 --> 01:03:17,529
So this dead dude from thirty
years ago, he is not so dead?

1076
01:03:17,552 --> 01:03:19,472
How could Stu Macher
really be alive?

1077
01:03:20,049 --> 01:03:21,489
Where's he been? Under a rock?

1078
01:03:21,618 --> 01:03:23,441
Nobody recognized him
for three decades?

1079
01:03:23,569 --> 01:03:26,256
That's a ridiculous retcon
for any franchise.

1080
01:03:26,386 --> 01:03:29,136
See, this time it is
all about nostalgia.

1081
01:03:29,266 --> 01:03:31,345
Hey, Min! We talked about
the rules thing,

1082
01:03:31,474 --> 01:03:33,435
we said we weren't gonna
do that anymore. We're better
than that. So just...

1083
01:03:33,458 --> 01:03:37,138
Okay. Whoever it is
wants to bring Sidney
out of retirement.

1084
01:03:37,265 --> 01:03:40,082
She's a scream queen.
Scream queens are not allowed
to have happy endings.

1085
01:03:40,209 --> 01:03:43,825
There's a reason they
keep putting Jamie Lee
in new Halloween movies.

1086
01:03:43,954 --> 01:03:46,010
We all want to read
Wuthering Heights
again for the first time.

1087
01:03:46,033 --> 01:03:47,442
But this is real life.

1088
01:03:47,569 --> 01:03:49,232
Yes, exactly.

1089
01:03:49,362 --> 01:03:51,665
This person isn't a fan of
Stab movies,

1090
01:03:51,793 --> 01:03:54,096
they're a fan of
Sidney Prescott.

1091
01:03:54,226 --> 01:03:55,856
Not the Sidney of today, though.

1092
01:03:55,985 --> 01:03:58,289
The Sidney of thirty years ago.

1093
01:03:58,418 --> 01:04:01,234
The Sidney that was killing
Ghostfaces, like, once a year.

1094
01:04:01,360 --> 01:04:03,665
And the reason they're using
Stu Macher to fuck with her

1095
01:04:03,793 --> 01:04:06,256
is because he was
there at the start.

1096
01:04:06,385 --> 01:04:10,000
The night Sidney the
Avenging Angel was born.

1097
01:04:11,825 --> 01:04:14,106
Or it really is Stu.
I mean, Billy Loomis
had a secret love child,

1098
01:04:14,129 --> 01:04:15,856
so who the fuck knows anymore?

1099
01:04:15,985 --> 01:04:17,425
Where'd you get these calls?
Uh...

1100
01:04:17,554 --> 01:04:20,849
My mom's cloud. Can you
tell if they're fake or not?

1101
01:04:20,976 --> 01:04:22,319
If it's a fake,
it's a good one.
Hmm.

1102
01:04:22,385 --> 01:04:24,017
The shadows are consistent.

1103
01:04:24,145 --> 01:04:27,409
The eyes, hands, they all have
zero artifacts or pixilation.
I mean...

1104
01:04:27,536 --> 01:04:28,764
These might have
been live calls.

1105
01:04:28,882 --> 01:04:31,602
All right, well,
if it is Stu Macher

1106
01:04:31,729 --> 01:04:33,713
then we know
he has an accomplice.

1107
01:04:33,842 --> 01:04:36,337
He can't be in two
places at once, so...

1108
01:04:37,778 --> 01:04:39,120
who is it?

1109
01:04:39,250 --> 01:04:41,114
Why would any of us want to
terrorize Tatum and her mom?

1110
01:04:41,137 --> 01:04:44,402
Why indeed. Let's talk motive.

1111
01:04:44,528 --> 01:04:45,970
Pardon. Thank you.

1112
01:04:46,097 --> 01:04:48,242
Okay, Ben.
Mmm.

1113
01:04:48,368 --> 01:04:50,897
Does Sidney truly approve
of you as Tatum's boyfriend?

1114
01:04:51,025 --> 01:04:54,512
Moms never like the boyfriend.
That's Mommy 101, there.

1115
01:04:54,642 --> 01:04:57,522
And you're an interesting
mix of brawn and brains.

1116
01:04:57,649 --> 01:05:00,080
Nah. I like to work out
my body and my mind, yeah.

1117
01:05:00,209 --> 01:05:01,973
See, that's incredibly
bizarre to say out loud.

1118
01:05:02,033 --> 01:05:03,665
Chloe.

1119
01:05:03,793 --> 01:05:05,522
- Hey.
- Fun-loving. Everyone likes.

1120
01:05:05,648 --> 01:05:08,017
Excellent hair.
Seemingly has no motive.

1121
01:05:08,146 --> 01:05:09,329
That's me.

1122
01:05:09,458 --> 01:05:10,609
- I'm not buying it.
- Good.

1123
01:05:10,736 --> 01:05:12,232
I don't like a girl
that everyone likes.

1124
01:05:12,338 --> 01:05:13,616
It's boring.

1125
01:05:13,746 --> 01:05:15,922
Oh. See? That's motive.

1126
01:05:16,049 --> 01:05:18,673
Right? Boredom? Now we're
in Stu Macher territory.

1127
01:05:18,802 --> 01:05:20,722
And you, weird boy.
Okay.

1128
01:05:20,849 --> 01:05:24,337
You've displayed
an unsettling obsession with
all things Sidney Prescott.

1129
01:05:24,466 --> 01:05:26,257
She's a pinnacle in
the true-crime lexicon.

1130
01:05:26,386 --> 01:05:27,856
I'm not obsessed.
I'm just...

1131
01:05:27,984 --> 01:05:30,800
I'm, uh, fascinated.

1132
01:05:30,929 --> 01:05:33,362
Splitting hairs, young man.

1133
01:05:33,488 --> 01:05:34,736
Okay, my money's on boyfriend.

1134
01:05:34,866 --> 01:05:36,209
Yeah, my bet's on creepy kid.

1135
01:05:36,338 --> 01:05:37,565
Okay, I'm pretty fucking sick of

1136
01:05:37,680 --> 01:05:39,248
all this "creepy" shit,
all right?

1137
01:05:39,376 --> 01:05:40,786
I'm not creepy.

1138
01:05:40,913 --> 01:05:42,962
Creepy is kind of hot.

1139
01:05:45,104 --> 01:05:46,642
Oh.
Hey.

1140
01:05:46,769 --> 01:05:47,953
Hey.

1141
01:05:49,040 --> 01:05:50,482
Can I have another beer?

1142
01:05:50,609 --> 01:05:52,049
You can have whatever you want.

1143
01:05:55,505 --> 01:05:58,097
And per our discussion,
this is my exclusive.

1144
01:05:58,225 --> 01:06:00,017
- That was the deal.
- Yeah, yeah. Got it.

1145
01:06:00,145 --> 01:06:02,258
- Okay.
- There you go.

1146
01:06:02,384 --> 01:06:03,600
Oh, okay.

1147
01:06:03,730 --> 01:06:05,264
Oh. There.

1148
01:06:06,577 --> 01:06:08,209
All right,
I have three cameras on you.

1149
01:06:08,336 --> 01:06:10,000
We'll be operating from
the control room.

1150
01:06:10,129 --> 01:06:12,785
We need your phone,
so when he calls...

1151
01:06:13,393 --> 01:06:15,505
Thank you.
All right, ladies,

1152
01:06:15,633 --> 01:06:19,217
we'll be ready to break into
every affiliate in the state
on your go.

1153
01:06:19,856 --> 01:06:21,970
Jesus, this is fucking awesome!

1154
01:06:22,576 --> 01:06:23,664
Okay.

1155
01:06:23,793 --> 01:06:25,841
Let's just hope that
Stu is watching.

1156
01:06:26,320 --> 01:06:27,313
Ready?

1157
01:06:27,440 --> 01:06:29,456
You gonna play nice?
Of course not.

1158
01:06:29,586 --> 01:06:32,626
I've been waiting for this
interview for thirty years.

1159
01:06:32,753 --> 01:06:34,193
And three, two...

1160
01:06:36,241 --> 01:06:40,625
Hi, I'm Gale Weathers
here for an exclusive interview
with Sidney Prescott.

1161
01:06:44,624 --> 01:06:45,937
What the hell?

1162
01:06:46,066 --> 01:06:48,913
My mom's going live on TV.
Channel 7.

1163
01:06:49,042 --> 01:06:50,033
Oh.

1164
01:06:52,721 --> 01:06:55,025
Welcome, Sidney. Hi.
Hi, Gale.

1165
01:06:55,153 --> 01:06:59,216
So everyone knows you as
the survivor of
many brutal attacks.

1166
01:06:59,346 --> 01:07:03,569
And I understand that
you and your family
are once again a target.

1167
01:07:03,698 --> 01:07:05,618
Can you explain
what's happening?

1168
01:07:05,744 --> 01:07:07,664
My family and I
have been attacked twice now

1169
01:07:07,793 --> 01:07:10,322
by someone claiming to be
Stu Macher.

1170
01:07:10,448 --> 01:07:12,464
But Stu was killed in Woodsboro

1171
01:07:12,593 --> 01:07:15,504
the night that he
and Billy Loomis attacked you.

1172
01:07:15,633 --> 01:07:19,153
Yes, but now I'm not so sure.

1173
01:07:19,280 --> 01:07:21,200
Is that why you're doing
this interview?

1174
01:07:21,330 --> 01:07:24,016
I want to talk to him.
What would you
like to say?

1175
01:07:24,144 --> 01:07:26,577
I want to know what he wants.

1176
01:07:26,705 --> 01:07:29,362
Why he's doing this
after all of these years.

1177
01:07:29,489 --> 01:07:31,090
I want him to know that

1178
01:07:31,985 --> 01:07:33,584
this doesn't need to continue.

1179
01:07:33,713 --> 01:07:35,345
Zoom in.
Tighter, tighter.

1180
01:07:35,473 --> 01:07:37,745
Whatever you need, let's talk.

1181
01:07:37,873 --> 01:07:38,866
Hmm.

1182
01:07:39,985 --> 01:07:42,098
Maybe he's too much of
a little bitch.

1183
01:07:42,897 --> 01:07:45,649
He always was the sidekick,
never the lead.

1184
01:07:47,762 --> 01:07:49,201
Is that what it is?

1185
01:07:49,330 --> 01:07:52,529
You want to be the lead?
Well, here you go.

1186
01:07:52,658 --> 01:07:54,449
Call me. You have a platform.

1187
01:07:54,578 --> 01:07:55,890
Oh, shit.

1188
01:07:59,953 --> 01:08:03,376
Maybe he hasn't tuned in yet.
Let's keep talking.

1189
01:08:04,336 --> 01:08:06,610
You and I have known
each other a long time.

1190
01:08:07,345 --> 01:08:09,040
A very long time, yes.

1191
01:08:09,168 --> 01:08:11,088
How would you describe
our relationship?

1192
01:08:12,145 --> 01:08:14,033
Complicated but enduring.

1193
01:08:15,153 --> 01:08:17,010
You wrote a book,
Out of Darkness,

1194
01:08:17,137 --> 01:08:18,930
about healing your trauma.

1195
01:08:19,057 --> 01:08:21,488
And yet you have
completely disappeared

1196
01:08:21,616 --> 01:08:24,145
from the public eye
for years now. Why?

1197
01:08:24,273 --> 01:08:28,049
It just seemed
the more I talked about it,
the more darkness came.

1198
01:08:28,178 --> 01:08:29,138
Mmm.

1199
01:08:29,264 --> 01:08:30,417
You have three children.

1200
01:08:30,545 --> 01:08:32,913
Tatum being your oldest.
She's seventeen?

1201
01:08:33,040 --> 01:08:34,609
I'd rather not talk about
my children.

1202
01:08:34,737 --> 01:08:38,290
Tatum is the same age
that you were
when this whole thing started.

1203
01:08:38,417 --> 01:08:40,433
That must have
a huge significance for you.

1204
01:08:40,562 --> 01:08:42,768
Like I said, I don't want to
talk about my kids.

1205
01:08:42,897 --> 01:08:44,913
And you named your kid Tatum

1206
01:08:45,041 --> 01:08:48,657
after the young girl who was
brutally murdered
all those years ago.

1207
01:08:48,785 --> 01:08:52,497
I named her after a childhood
friend whom I loved dearly.

1208
01:08:54,192 --> 01:08:56,561
She was the last friend
I ever trusted.

1209
01:08:58,353 --> 01:08:59,345
Mmm.

1210
01:09:00,016 --> 01:09:01,205
Sidney, do you ever worry about

1211
01:09:01,233 --> 01:09:03,377
passing your trauma on
to your children?

1212
01:09:03,505 --> 01:09:04,720
Or, even worse yet,

1213
01:09:04,848 --> 01:09:06,690
that they would be
the target of future killings?

1214
01:09:06,768 --> 01:09:07,921
Oh, shit.

1215
01:09:08,050 --> 01:09:09,970
Sidney?
Okay, Gale, stop.

1216
01:09:12,242 --> 01:09:14,737
Where's she going?
Okay, we'll be right back.

1217
01:09:14,866 --> 01:09:17,073
Or maybe not. Cut.

1218
01:09:17,200 --> 01:09:18,224
All right.

1219
01:09:18,354 --> 01:09:20,305
Um... Go to the outro
and stand by.

1220
01:09:20,433 --> 01:09:22,257
Wh...

1221
01:09:24,722 --> 01:09:25,969
That was unfair.

1222
01:09:26,386 --> 01:09:28,049
And dangerous!

1223
01:09:28,177 --> 01:09:30,545
But you disappeared, Sid.
People want to know.

1224
01:09:30,672 --> 01:09:32,177
I want to know!

1225
01:09:32,977 --> 01:09:34,930
I'm sorry.
Are you?

1226
01:09:35,057 --> 01:09:38,257
What if I had asked you
about Dewey on live TV?

1227
01:09:38,384 --> 01:09:39,343
What would you say?

1228
01:09:39,409 --> 01:09:41,681
Well, I'd say I'm fine.

1229
01:09:42,929 --> 01:09:46,000
Because that's what I
tell myself 500 times a day

1230
01:09:46,129 --> 01:09:48,145
just to get through the day.

1231
01:10:07,152 --> 01:10:09,937
This has been a Robbie Rivers
exclusive with Gale Weathers

1232
01:10:10,064 --> 01:10:12,817
and Pine Grove's very
own Sidney Prescott Evans.

1233
01:10:12,977 --> 01:10:14,353
We will be monitoring...

1234
01:10:14,481 --> 01:10:16,177
That was intense.

1235
01:10:17,617 --> 01:10:18,801
Yeah.

1236
01:10:19,442 --> 01:10:20,624
Are you okay?

1237
01:10:23,472 --> 01:10:25,009
I'm sorry this is happening.

1238
01:10:25,681 --> 01:10:28,082
And this...
This was a dumb idea.

1239
01:10:28,208 --> 01:10:29,425
How far is the TV station?

1240
01:10:29,553 --> 01:10:31,317
I just really want to be with
my mom right now.

1241
01:10:31,409 --> 01:10:33,169
We're super close.
I mean, I'll take you.

1242
01:10:33,649 --> 01:10:34,897
Okay.

1243
01:10:41,522 --> 01:10:42,640
We're not on air.

1244
01:10:42,769 --> 01:10:44,625
And this needs to be
on air.
Hello?

1245
01:10:44,753 --> 01:10:47,281
Aw, Sid, do you need a hug?

1246
01:10:48,913 --> 01:10:50,385
We've been waiting for you.

1247
01:10:50,513 --> 01:10:51,664
Why? So I can
stay on the phone

1248
01:10:51,697 --> 01:10:53,114
long enough for you to
trace the call?

1249
01:10:53,137 --> 01:10:55,793
Yes, dumbass! Or you could
just tell us where you are.

1250
01:10:55,921 --> 01:10:58,673
Great. I am at Parker's Tavern

1251
01:10:58,801 --> 01:11:00,465
with your daughter.

1252
01:11:01,201 --> 01:11:02,705
My daughter's not at Parker's.

1253
01:11:02,833 --> 01:11:04,369
Well, she's definitely not
at home.

1254
01:11:04,497 --> 01:11:06,161
She broke curfew.

1255
01:11:06,289 --> 01:11:08,050
She's a bad bitch.

1256
01:11:08,593 --> 01:11:10,033
I'm gonna punish her.

1257
01:11:10,993 --> 01:11:12,177
Fuck.

1258
01:11:12,305 --> 01:11:13,681
Is that it?
Is he gonna call back?

1259
01:11:13,810 --> 01:11:15,248
Because you said
this was my story.

1260
01:11:15,377 --> 01:11:16,489
Where's the story, Gale?
Stop!

1261
01:11:16,561 --> 01:11:18,289
You need to
call the police right now,

1262
01:11:18,417 --> 01:11:20,529
tell them to go to
Parker's Tavern.

1263
01:11:21,169 --> 01:11:22,353
Sidney!

1264
01:11:23,633 --> 01:11:25,009
Sidney!

1265
01:11:25,777 --> 01:11:26,929
Oh, fuck.

1266
01:11:27,057 --> 01:11:28,945
Mark, Tatum went
to Chloe's restaurant.

1267
01:11:29,073 --> 01:11:30,161
She's in trouble.

1268
01:11:30,289 --> 01:11:31,505
Where are you?

1269
01:11:31,633 --> 01:11:32,592
Damn it!

1270
01:11:36,337 --> 01:11:37,521
Oh, fuck.

1271
01:11:48,017 --> 01:11:49,201
Thanks.

1272
01:11:58,641 --> 01:11:59,953
What is this?
Hmm?

1273
01:12:00,081 --> 01:12:01,361
Oh, uh...

1274
01:12:01,489 --> 01:12:04,369
- Did you create this?
- What? No.

1275
01:12:04,497 --> 01:12:06,641
I created that one just
to see if it was possible.

1276
01:12:06,769 --> 01:12:09,137
I can't wait to fucking
kill you, Sidney Prescott,

1277
01:12:09,265 --> 01:12:10,673
and your daughter.

1278
01:12:10,801 --> 01:12:14,161
And I'm gonna love
every second of it, you bitch!

1279
01:12:14,289 --> 01:12:15,025
Tate.

1280
01:12:15,153 --> 01:12:17,521
It was you.
No, it wasn't.

1281
01:12:19,345 --> 01:12:20,849
Tate.

1282
01:12:33,361 --> 01:12:35,537
You know, not exactly
a roaring success, Min.

1283
01:12:35,665 --> 01:12:37,489
We still have no idea
who the killer is.

1284
01:12:37,617 --> 01:12:39,281
Creepy kid still has my vote.

1285
01:12:39,409 --> 01:12:40,465
I'm way too obvious.

1286
01:12:40,593 --> 01:12:42,801
So obvious it's not obvious.

1287
01:12:42,929 --> 01:12:44,498
What is that smell?

1288
01:12:45,073 --> 01:12:48,049
Oh, shit! Pizza's in the oven.

1289
01:12:50,416 --> 01:12:51,921
Bathroom break.

1290
01:12:54,993 --> 01:12:58,321
We should not have left Tatum
alone with Gen-Z Billy Loomis.

1291
01:12:58,449 --> 01:12:59,921
Okay? I'm not feeling good
about that.

1292
01:13:00,049 --> 01:13:02,417
Do you find it weird
that two very real suspects

1293
01:13:02,544 --> 01:13:03,695
just conveniently disappeared?

1294
01:13:04,561 --> 01:13:06,010
I really don't want
to get stabbed tonight.

